{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>In the second year. And the children of Israel performed the Passover, etc.</b> In the first chapter of Pesaḥim the Gemara asks why Scripture placed the passage of ״שאו את ראש בני ישראל״ at the beginning of the book before this passage here — for this event was earlier, for here it is written ״בחדש הראשון״, which is Nisan, and there it is written ״באחד לחדש השני״, which is Iyyar. And it answers: there is no earlier and later in the Torah. Even so, one can give a reason for the matter: because all the priestly Torah was in the Tent of Meeting, and there too it is written ״באהל מועד״, and adjacent to that passage it speaks of the standards and their encampments, which were around the Tabernacle — therefore it placed it earlier. And Rashi explained that Scripture did not begin the book with this passage because it saw that it speaks to the discredit of Israel, that they performed only this one Passover all those forty years that Israel were in the wilderness. And if you ask: what discredit is this? For upon entry into the land the verse suspended it, as it is said: ״והיה כי יביאך״ etc. ״ועבדת את העבודה הזאת״, and moreover this Passover too they would not have offered except by divine command — one can say that the discredit is that if they had merited and not sinned, they would have entered the land in the second year, and would have performed Passover every single year."], :book :numbers, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 9, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:09:05.029757626Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}